{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/648900-kinain-mages","id":648900,"title":"Kinain mages","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-02T06:58:45-07:00","id":648900,"title":"Kinain mages","content":"Hey folks,<br /> <br /> So I'm reading up on kinain mages, and there are a few contradictory systems. There's the Faerie Affinity Merit, the Fae Blood Merit and then the system for kinain in The Enchanted (which would appear to be just for unawakened mortals).<br /> <br /> I'm wondering how Mage STs manage this? Do you allow PCs to take Fae Gifts and Fae Marks? What about Kinain Backgrounds? Can they or can they not use cantrips (my feeling is that Awakened mages can't use Glamour, which prevents them using cantrips)?<br /> <br /> I posted this in the general CWoD forum, but no one replied, so thought I'd try here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T11:20:42-07:00","id":649130,"title":"","content":"There's a character in my chronicle with Fae Blood. I allow him to do the following: enter the Dreaming with Spirit 3, learn cantrips (one per Arete dot, cost 1 quintessence per use, no Paradox), have low Banality (2-5), perceive Chimera with Mind 1/Spirit 1, and harvest Glamour with Prime 3/Spirit 3 (up to 5 points, treated as Quintessence with appropriate Resonance). He is also subject to Ravaging (losing his fae blood powers for one day per point ravaged).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2543-thebian","name":"Thebian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2543_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T12:59:22-07:00","id":649232,"title":"","content":"I imagine mind 3 is rather terrifying to changelings. Illusions are pretty real to the fae","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>there are no bad ideas, just ideas that have not been refined enough","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1608-iamthesweeper","name":"IAmTheSweeper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1608_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T14:29:09-07:00","id":649312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thebian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/648900-kinain-mages?p=649130#post649130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a character in my chronicle with Fae Blood. I allow him to do the following: enter the Dreaming with Spirit 3, learn cantrips (one per Arete dot, cost 1 quintessence per use, no Paradox), have low Banality (2-5), perceive Chimera with Mind 1/Spirit 1, and harvest Glamour with Prime 3/Spirit 3 (up to 5 points, treated as Quintessence with appropriate Resonance). He is also subject to Ravaging (losing his fae blood powers for one day per point ravaged).</div> </div> </div> </div>This is quite interesting. I have so far ruled that cantrips can be used as rotes, provided the character has the relevant Spheres to do so normally. I know the developers have said, in the past, that fae beings are cut off from Awakening, because their Avatars are suppressed by the spiritual connection to the Dreaming. However, if mages can't use cantrips, then it begs the question of whether they can have Fae Gifts either...<br /> <br /> Any more thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T14:52:47-07:00","id":649340,"title":"","content":"I'm not particularly experienced with Changeling, and I'd probably need to do a lot more reading before I had a Fae Blood character in one of my games. But that said, I think that Fae Gifts could be workable depending on the Gift in question.<br /> <br /> I think that I would first discuss the nature of the character's fae blood on character creation, and have the player choose spheres that fit accordingly with the nature of the fae ancestry and the gift that he wants the character to have. If, for example, the player wanted the gift to speak to spirits of the dead, I might not give him the Gift outright, but I would expect him to have significantly invested in the Spirit and Entropy spheres, and I would reduce difficulty of any efforts at dealing with the Wraith and the Underworld. I would also remove Paradox as a factor with regard to the &quot;gift&quot; within reason. (I always reserve the right to tell my players &quot;Okay, you're taking this a little too far.&quot; :-))","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T16:29:38-07:00","id":649514,"title":"","content":"In our game, the mage in question doesn't have fae blood because he's related to changelings from Changeling: the Dreaming per se. Instead, he is an ancient umbrood that has &quot;fallen&quot; into the material world (because reasons), so, as kalinara says, the nature of the character's fae blood is central to the concept. This sidesteps any crossovers issues (&quot;but Changelings can't...&quot;) and allows us to use Changeling material to model our ideas without being tied to canonical elements from C:tD.<br /> <br /> And yeah, illusions and the like are a central element of the character's life. He also has the Nightmares flaw and the Addiction (cocaine) flaw. These manifest as Chimera/Nocnitsa that cause him all sorts of unpleasantness. Laughing Charlie, his cocaine chimera, is particularly odious. I suspect the character is planning to kill Charlie as a way of removing the flaw, which will be fun to play out <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2543-thebian","name":"Thebian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2543_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T04:58:17-07:00","id":649957,"title":"","content":"A cocaine chimera called Laughing Charlie? I love that so much!<br /> <br /> Here's the stuff I wrote for the RPoL wiki for our game. Can anyone offer any feedback?<br /> <br /> Glamour and cantrips: Sorcerers, psychics and mages can all be kinain. However, only unawakened kinain may use cantrips (and may take traits in Arts, Realms and Glamour) as they are under the system in The Enchanted. An Awakened mage cannot have a Glamour rating (because being tied to the Dreaming would prevent their Avatar from Awakening), but can learn cantrips as if they were rotes, and power them through Spheres.* Similarly, any Fae Gift or Background that requires the use of a Glamour trait is off-limits to mage characters (Fith-Fath, Riastradh, etc), but rotes can be developed to provide similar powers with Spheres.<br /> <br /> Character creation: The character creation rules in The Enchanted are for mortal kinain only. You should create your character as a mage or hedge mage first, and then use Freebies to 'add on' the fae characteristics. You should consult The Enchanted for the specific rules on kinain-specific traits.<br /> <br /> Apply the following template to modify your kinain character:<br /> <br /> 1. Create a mage/hedge mage character as normal, remembering that chimerical reality and/or their fae blood will be incorporated into their paradigm. The character's Avatar essence might also be informed by their fae heritage (a Sluagh-descended kinain may be Primordial, while a Satyr's relative may be Dynamic).<br /> <br /> 2. Take the 4-point Merit: Faerie Blood. This will grant the character a single dot in the Faerie Blood Background. Alternatively, you can take the Faerie Affinity Merit, which gives you a lower Banality (one dot lower than normal) and makes changelings more friendly, but does not allow the character to take any Fae Gifts or Kinain Backgrounds, nor to interact with chimerical reality.<br /> <br /> 3. Note your Seeming and Seelie/Unseelie Legacies. Pick a Heritage (Kith). Your Banality rating will be the lower of: a) the Banality rating for your Seeming in The Enchanted; or b) the Banality rating as defined in the Character Creation for Mages section (I use the lower scale presented in CTD, where mages have Banality ratings of 2-7 for the most part).<br /> <br /> 4. You start with no free Fae Gifts or Kinain Backgrounds. You can spend Freebies to take any Fae Gifts and Kinain Backgrounds you like (provided you already have the Faerie Blood Merit), but you may not take more dots in either of these than you have dots in the Faerie Blood Background. So if you have Faerie Blood 5, you can take up to five separate Fae Gifts and up to five separate Kinain Backgrounds. These tricks are Paradox-free. Kinain Backgrounds can only be bought from your Freebie pool, rather than from your normal Background dots.<br /> <br /> 5. Fae Marks can be taken to gain additional Freebie Points.<br /> <br /> *In general, awakened mages who mimic cantrips can consider chimerical effects to be coincidental and Wyrd effects to be vulgar. Hedge mages never take Paradox from cantrips, of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 09-03-2015, 08:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T05:27:01-07:00","id":649976,"title":"","content":"Addendum: I'd probably clarify the overlap between Glamour and Quintessence, too. For example, an item can contain (or, more correctly, generate) Glamour without holding Quintessence. A picture, for example, would inspire Glamour that a changeling could harvest. But a mage looking at the same picture wouldn't be able to harvest Quintessence (they'd have to wait for the changeling to harvest the Glamour and then steal it from the changeling).<br /> <br /> Similarly, a site of Quintessence might not generate Glamour in the same way as a freehold would for a changeling. The changeling would probably draw much less Glamour from a node than a mage would draw Quintessence, for example, because it's not in the form she's used to receiving it in. However, a mage could easily draw the Glamour from a freehold as Quintessence, albeit Quintessence with a particular Resonance (and the potential to cause side-effects), because mages don't really require their Quintessence to be refined.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T12:04:21-07:00","id":650403,"title":"","content":"Hm, a parallel for the Glamour/Quintessence separation might be the Syndicate's Primal Utility: it lets you use economic activity and Resources as a source of Quint, while those with regular Prime won't even register it as a source.<br /> <br /> So you might consider having an alternate Prime or Prime/Mind Minor Sphere that Fae-blooded Mages can take, which focuses on harvesting and manipulation of Glamour and Glamour-based constructs. At the cost of having difficulty manipulating or recognizing non-chimeric Quintessence sources (and a 'conversion' ability at probably Glamour 4 which lets you change the Resonance to convert other types of Quintessence into Glamour).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T14:25:53-07:00","id":650580,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of a Glamour Minor Sphere, actually. I might offer that at half price for mages who want to focus especially on Glamour. Or maybe it can be Fae, after the Realm of the same name in Changeling, and govern similar principles (the manipulation of the Dreaming and beings from the Dreaming).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T13:39:53-08:00","id":822695,"title":"","content":"I love the idea of a kinain wizard. Maybe the first step should to be playtesting a kinain hedge wizard/sorcerer. <br /> <br /> About the idea of a mage with aret\u00e9, spheres, glamour, arts and realms... too complicate... but if we create a new fellowship (dark age: mage) with his own pillars and fundations. <br /> <br /> My suggestion is:<br /> <br /> Kinain edge wizard with arts and realms but not a true awakened.<br /> <br /> Awakakened with fae blood, with aret\u00e9 and spheres, or pillars and fundations, and even with glamour/banality levels but without arts and realms. This faetouched mage could use chimerical item. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T22:02:55-07:00","id":1220183,"title":"","content":"I don't know if it's still a thing, but I vaguely remember that quintessence could be harvested from glamour with prime, mind and spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23984-thkaal","name":"Thkaal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-19T05:23:43-07:00","id":1220231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thkaal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/648900-kinain-mages?p=1220183#post1220183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know if it's still a thing, but I vaguely remember that quintessence could be harvested from glamour with prime, mind and spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Vitae, Gnosis, Glamour and other &quot;fuel sources&quot; can all be made into Quitessence... most reliably through nasty methods which consume the supernatural in question, and taint the resonance, since few Supernaturals give up power willingly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-19T11:32:54-07:00","id":1220287,"title":"","content":"Arise, necrothread! Arise!<br /> <br /> <br /> On topic, when it comes to Merits that blend a Mage with another splat (Ghoul, Shapeshifter Kin, Fae Blooded, Medium, etc), I gravitate towards the option described in the Mage Revised Storyteller's Handbook. That being that the Mage is able to exploit the Mythic Threads created by their connection, and use Spheres to create Effects that mirror those powers ascribed to the night folk by popular culture. And have those Effects be Coincidental. I would personally rather use that option in a Mage game, rather than having the characters track their understanding of a whole other splat's supernatural advantages. It's easier from a book-keeping and systems perspective, and sidesteps the need to split experience between different kinds of powers. The mage is a Mage, and thus does everything using their Spheres.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-19T12:07:21-07:00","id":1220300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/648900-kinain-mages?p=1220287#post1220287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Arise, necrothread! Arise!<br /> <br /> <br /> On topic, when it comes to Merits that blend a Mage with another splat (Ghoul, Shapeshifter Kin, Fae Blooded, Medium, etc), I gravitate towards the option described in the Mage Revised Storyteller's Handbook. That being that the Mage is able to exploit the Mythic Threads created by their connection, and use Spheres to create Effects that mirror those powers ascribed to the night folk by popular culture. And have those Effects be Coincidental. I would personally rather use that option in a Mage game, rather than having the characters track their understanding of a whole other splat's supernatural advantages. It's easier from a book-keeping and systems perspective, and sidesteps the need to split experience between different kinds of powers. The mage is a Mage, and thus does everything using their Spheres.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with this for complex powers, and the Nephalim merit can always capture other strange associations.<br /> <br /> However powers like Potence, or a single Werewolf Gift, can be much simpler than some Merits and Backgrounds in Mage. I would simply make sure that the character isn't going to expand too far into these powers, and buy more and more in-game. It will harm their power potential (honestly; I mean buying Celerity 2 is neat but that's 15 EXP you could have spent on Spheres Ghouly Boi) in the long run and make them feel less like a Mage, while also adding more bookkeeping in some cases.<br /> <br /> But a single unique power (as in powers outside of Spheres), or a few, at Character Generation feels nice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}